'''Manta Air''' is a Maldivian airline based in the [[Maldives]], which began its operations on 24 February 2019. It began international operations in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://mantaair.mv/news/manta-air-starts-its-operations |title=Manta Air officially begins its operations today! |date=2019-02-24 |website=www.mantaair.mv |language=en-US |access-date=2019-06-21}}</ref>

== History ==
Manta Air had its first aircraft delivered on 12 November 2018,<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://mantaair.mv/news/manta-air-welcomes-its-first-edition-to-its-fleet|title=Manta Air Welcomes its First Addition to its Fleet|website=Manta Air Welcomes its First Addition to its Fleet &#124; Manta Air|access-date=Apr 15, 2021}}</ref> and the airline was unveiled to the Maldives on 22 November 2018 by the Vice President of the Maldives, [[Faisal Naseem]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://mantaair.mv/news/manta-air-s-brand-officially-launched-in-the-maldives|title=Manta Air launches {{as written|i|t's [sic]}} brand officially in the Maldives|website=mantaair.mv|access-date=Apr 15, 2021}}</ref>

Manta Air received the [[Air Operator's Certificate]] on 21 February 2019 and officially started its operations on 24 February 2019.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://maldives.net.mv/29857/manta-air-begins-flight-operations/|title=Manta Air begins flight operations|date=Feb 24, 2019|access-date=Apr 15, 2021}}</ref>

Manta Air began its float-plane (seaplane) operations on 17 November 2019.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://avas.mv/en/73439 |title=Manta Air begins seaplane operation with inauguration of new terminal. |date=2019-11-18 |website=www.avas.mv/en |language=en-US |access-date=2019-11-18}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://edition.mv/business/13497 |title=Manta Air commences seaplane flights, opens terminal. |date=2019-11-18 |website=www.edition.mv |language=en-US |access-date=2019-11-18}}</ref>

